# {{.Name}}

This independent Go module is {{.Module}}. It requires Go {{.GoVersion}} or later
and pins Fathomry to {{.FrameworkVersion}}. The project and Fathomry compile into
one application named fathomry; there is no separate CLI proxy. The project name
identifies the application, not a different executable or command implementation.
This profile implements configuration checking, not a Worker or workflow executor.

The pinned framework revision provides RunProject and the application
configuration APIs. Changing it requires requalifying the template/API pair;
no arbitrary-version compatibility is promised.

## Project structure

| Location | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| main.go | Process signals, standard streams and exit status |
| internal/bootstrap | Connect project declarations to the shared Fathomry commands |
| internal/setting | Complete Config, Application, typed defaults and pure validation |
| .env | Bootstrap selection and startup budgets; ignored by Git |
| .env.example | Non-secret bootstrap example, also used by project tests |
| config/base.yaml | Shared application values |
| config/environment/ | Explicit environment overrides; only the selected file is loaded |

Add database.go, cache.go or other configuration sections under internal/setting
when the project uses those capabilities, and include them in Config. Keep clients,
file/network access and lifecycle ownership out of configuration structs.

setting.Schema returns the Framework-owned configuration.Schema[Config].
Bootstrap only supplies declarations and explicitly captured startup facts to the
shared command entry. It does not call configsource preparation or construct
configuration-center clients. The framework owns that translation and loading.

Application groups Build, Deployment and Instance alongside name, display_name,
description, business namespace, timezone and existing i18n preferences. Build
contains version/revision/built_at; Deployment contains environment/region/zone/cluster.
An unspecified location stays empty instead of inventing a production region.
Application namespace is not a Kubernetes namespace or tenant authorization.

The project schema factory runs once after bootstrap admission. It supplies the
selected environment and captures FATHOMRY_INSTANCE_ID from the process; absence
creates a random startup ID, while explicit empty rejects. This is a declared
project input, not another permitted dotenv key. Build metadata is compiled into
internal/bootstrap (version defaults to devel; revision/builtAt are unknown).
Application files cannot override these startup-owned fields.

To stamp an artifact, supply actual CI values through -ldflags -X for
{{.Module}}/internal/bootstrap.version, .revision and .builtAt (using the full
package prefix for each). A nonempty builtAt must be a UTC RFC3339 timestamp.
Do not confuse application version with the Fathomry dependency or schema version.

## Resolve dependencies explicitly

Generation did not run Go, Git or service checks. Resolve dependencies yourself:

```sh
GOWORK=off go mod tidy
GOWORK=off go test ./...
GOWORK=off go run . --help
GOWORK=off go run . config check --output=json
```

Go creates go.sum and may add indirect requirements. Keep those files with your
project. Creation writes a non-secret .env; after cloning, copy .env.example to
.env yourself. Tests use .env.example, not a developer's private .env. Do not commit
credentials or copy Fathomry's local SDK replacement graph into this module.

## Configuration and startup

Help and invalid syntax do not load configuration. A configuration check:

1. Captures only declared bootstrap variables and reads the selected dotenv file
   under a finite early budget.
2. Admits the complete bootstrap before opening application configuration sources.
3. Loads, validates and accepts one complete application snapshot.
4. Closes owned sessions/resources and emits a bounded safe report on success.

The required bootstrap file defaults to ./.env relative to the working directory.
Use --bootstrap for an explicit path and --env for an environment override:

```sh
GOWORK=off go run . config check --env production
"$BUILD_OUTPUT/fathomry" config check --bootstrap /run/application/.env --output=json
```

Precedence is explicit flags, captured process variables, dotenv, then documented
defaults. Empty values are present, not absent. All supplied values are checked,
including shadowed values. Unknown dotenv keys reject. Dotenv is literal: no shell,
export, interpolation or process-environment mutation, and no Docker Compose syntax
compatibility promise. See Fathomry's configuration bootstrap reference for the
complete key inventory, remote Nacos profile and bounds.

The example explicitly selects development, local/Viper and Watch=false. Local
mode requires config/base.yaml and config/environment/<environment>.yaml relative
to the dotenv parent. Neither a missing file nor a rejected candidate falls back
to another environment/provider. The empty environment files contain valid YAML
mappings, not empty bytes. Application defaults and validation belong to setting.Schema.
The setting tests exercise pure data rules; bootstrap tests exercise actual
source-layer merging, rejected overrides and the independent config-check command.
Timezone defaults to UTC; validation checks bounded IANA-style identifier syntax
without consulting host files. A future time-consuming capability must resolve
that identifier against its chosen timezone catalog before use and reject unknown
names. This check does not certify timezone catalog availability or scheduling.
Do not mutate time.Local or reinterpret already-frozen task times.

Before reading dotenv, bootstrap acquisition and failure cleanup each default to
5s. Accepted bootstrap selects startup/candidate/shutdown budgets of 30s/5s/10s unless
overridden. Budgets are cooperative, not a way to kill blocked callbacks. The
configuration check remains finite with Watch=true: it accepts the observer's first
valid snapshot, then closes. It does not leave a watcher or certify service readiness.

Further commands must construct required capabilities only after configuration
acceptance and admit business work only after those capabilities are ready. No
database, cache, migration, registration or Worker startup is implied by this check.

## Build and run

Set BUILD_OUTPUT to an existing directory you own. Use a temporary-build area for
disposable experiments and a permanent artifact location for retained binaries.

```sh
test -n "$BUILD_OUTPUT" && test -d "$BUILD_OUTPUT" &&
  GOWORK=off go build -o "$BUILD_OUTPUT/fathomry" .
"$BUILD_OUTPUT/fathomry" --help
```

The binary embeds the CLI; it does not invoke a globally installed fathomry or
require Go/the original source directory at runtime. The binary owns application
exit codes; go run can wrap a failed program's exit status.
Install this application's binary on its deployment PATH to use fathomry directly.
Do not overwrite another application's same-named binary in a shared installation.

Debug the root package, not an individual file list. In GoLand, select a
Directory/Package run configuration at the project root. In VS Code Go, set
program and cwd to ${workspaceFolder}; pass config check as arguments. Running
go run . keeps future root-package files in the build, unlike go run main.go.

Build one binary/image and promote the same artifact across environments. Mount
versioned bootstrap/application files and inject Secrets explicitly at runtime;
exclude .env from the image build context. Use exec-form startup, standard streams,
non-root execution and explicit writable temporary storage with a read-only root.
Fathomry's project-deployment guide supplies container and configuration-check Job
examples; it does not provision infrastructure or qualify a real Kubernetes cluster.

Treat configuration checks as finite validation tasks, not liveness/readiness
probes. Bootstrap selection is not hot-reloaded. Watch updates preserve last-good
data but do not provide a multi-file transaction or automatic client rotation.

## Ownership and current limits

The generated files are project-owned and may be edited. Future template changes
do not overwrite them. No automatic updater, service discovery, registration,
database migration, workflow/Mode definition or deployment was generated.

The developer-only project-new command is not part of this project's command
profile. Build the official developer CLI from its supported source checkout;
versioned go install of the supplying Fathomry module currently rejects its local
replacement directives. Do not copy that replacement graph into this module.

Template notices describe the supplied source. No business-owner identity or
project-wide business license was selected on your behalf.
